        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Deus ingens infantulum induere volebat, parvum, tenellum, blandulum se terris exhibebat: ut cunctis sic amabilis foret, praesertim reis, non esset formidabilis, culpas indulgens eis: ridens blande nos aspicit suavi nos spe sic afficit.",
          "english": "The mighty God wished to put on the form of a little infant;\nHe showed Himself on earth little, tender, and gentle,\nThat He might thus be lovable to all, especially to sinners,\nAnd not dreadful, granting them pardon for their sins.\nSmiling gently, He looks upon us\nAnd thus fills us with sweet hope.",
          "sourcePages": [
            52
          ],
          "translation": {
