        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Puer in quo mirifice divinitas se celat, formae tamen deificae venustas te revelat: lucis divinae radius ex oculis dimanat, cor meum velut gladius amoris ictu tranat: amore quis det moriari, hac morte caelis oriar!",
          "english": "O Child, in whom the Godhead wondrously hides itself,\nYet the beauty of Thy divine form reveals Thee:\nA ray of divine light streams from Thine eyes\nAnd, like a sword, pierces my heart with the stroke of love.\nWho will grant that I may die of love,\nAnd through this death rise to heaven?",
          "sourcePages": [
            52
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              52
            ],
