        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Saepe cor meum angitur, sua volvens delicta. Vix non desperans frangitur, mens metu jacet icta: sed dum infantis cogito mei blandum amorem, dimitti culpas, rogito exutiens timorem. A se me non projiciet, propitius aspiciet.",
          "english": "Often my heart is distressed as it considers its sins.\nAlmost despairing, it is broken; my mind lies struck with fear.\nBut when I think upon the gentle love of my Infant,\nI ask that my sins be forgiven, casting away fear.\nHe will not cast me away from Himself;\nHe will look upon me graciously.",
