          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Dum frigore constringeris, qui ignis es divinus: totus rigore cingeris, meos veni in sinus. Cor meum ardens flammulis amoris te fovebit, a tuis nunquam famulis me ullus dimovebit: tenebo, nec dimittam te, donec mors advocabit me.",
          "english": "While Thou art bound by cold, Thou who art divine fire,\nAnd art wholly surrounded by freezing chill, come into my bosom.\nMy heart, burning with little flames of love, will warm Thee.\nNo one shall ever remove me from among Thy servants.\nI shall hold Thee and not let Thee go\nUntil death calls me.",
